course: dictionary
lesson: 4730
title: What is a hormone?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hormone is a chemical messenger. Your body makes it, it travels round in your blood, and it tells other parts of your body what to do. Think of it as a message delivered by the blood.
explain: «In deep sleep the body releases most of its growth hormone.» Growth hormone is a hormone that helps your body grow, and it is released mostly while you are in deep sleep.
explain: Plants have hormones too. They control how plants grow, such as making roots grow down and shoots grow towards the light.
fact: A hormone is a chemical messenger made in the body.
fact: Hormones travel in the blood and tell parts of the body what to do.
fact: Adrenaline is a hormone that makes your heart race when you are scared.
fact: Insulin is a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.
fact: Plants have hormones that control how they grow, such as making roots grow down.
exercise: What is a hormone? | A bone that holds up the body | *A chemical messenger made in the body that travels in the blood | A type of food high in sugar | A kind of muscle in the leg
exercise: Which hormone makes your heart race when you are scared? | Growth hormone | Insulin | *Adrenaline | Sugar
exercise: What do plant hormones do? | Carry blood round the stem | Turn leaves blue | *Control how plants grow, such as making roots grow down | Turn seeds into fish
test: When is most growth hormone released? | At lunchtime | *In deep sleep, mostly early in the night | During a maths test | When you are reading a book
test: Which hormone controls the sugar in the blood? | Adrenaline | *Insulin | Oxygen | Growth hormone
exam: Which best describes a hormone? | A part of the eye | A kind of rock found in the ground | A food the body eats | *A chemical messenger that travels in the blood and tells the body what to do
